course: dictionary
lesson: 11187
title: What is a wishbone?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wishbone is the forked, V-shaped bone between the neck and breast of a chicken, turkey or other bird. The clue is in «Snap the wishbone of the Sunday chicken»: you can snap it, so it is a real bone you can hold.
explain: Context tells you what a word means. «Pull the wishbone after a Sunday roast and you hold a bone T. rex had too» shows the wishbone is inside the bird, and that a dinosaur had the same bone. Pull and snap are clues that it is a bone you can break apart.
explain: A wishbone is also a game and a custom. Two people each pull one end, and the one with the bigger piece makes a wish. It is a game, not real magic.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A wishbone is a forked, V-shaped bone between the neck and breast of a chicken, turkey or other bird.
fact: «Wishbone» also names a game: two people pull it, and the one with the bigger piece makes a wish.
fact: The wishbone is two collarbones joined together.
fact: Birds use the wishbone like a spring when they flap their wings, and «T. rex» and «Velociraptor» had one too.
exercise: What is a wishbone? | *A forked, V-shaped bone between the neck and breast of a bird | A kind of dinosaur | A bird's beak | A bird's feather
exercise: In the wishbone game, who makes a wish? | The chicken | The bird's mum | *The person with the bigger piece | The person with the smaller piece
exercise: «The wishbone is two collarbones joined together.» What does joined mean? | Cooked | Painted | *Fixed or stuck together | Pulled apart
test: In «Birds and many dinosaurs share hollow bones, wishbones, three-toed feet and feathers.», which thing is shared? | Three-toed feet | Feathers | Chickens | *Wishbones
test: What does the wishbone help a bird do? | Sing loudly | Lay eggs | *Flap its wings and fly | Keep warm
exam: From «A chicken has two legs, two wings and two breasts; the wishbone is its two collarbones joined together.», what is a wishbone made of? | Two wings | Two breasts | *Two collarbones joined together | Two legs
